# Every test file `pnpm exec vitest list --filesOnly` must still execute, one
# web-relative path per line. Read by the step "Check typecheck covers every test
# file" in .github/workflows/ci.yml, which fails when a path recorded here is no
# longer in vitest's list. Order does not matter — the step sorts both sides — so
# add a line wherever you like; `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# A RATCHET, and one-sided: it asserts recorded is a subset of executed, so
# ADDING a test never reds CI and never requires touching this file. It is not
# the "count that goes red every time someone adds a file" the step's own comment
# rejects. What it makes impossible is a test file quietly LEAVING the suite.
#
# Nothing else in that step can see that. Rename `foo.test.ts` to `foo.ts` and it
# disappears from vitest's list AND from the git-index glob at the same time, so
# both sides of the subset assertion shrink together and it still passes — while
# the file stays inside the typecheck set, keeps compiling, and never runs again.
# Adding members to the coverage union cannot help: the file was never outside
# the coverage. Measured before this file existed, by renaming one spec in the
# index: the step printed `OK: all 14 test file(s) are inside the typecheck
# coverage set` and exited 0, its own reported number having just gone down.
#
# Paths and not a count, which was the first attempt at this. A count admits a
# compensating addition — rename one spec out of the suite and add an unrelated
# one in the same commit, and the total is unchanged and the removal is hidden
# (measured: green). A count also drifts, because nothing forces it upward: as
# this branch refills web/, a number recorded today sits further and further
# below the real one and stops detecting anything short of a mass deletion. A
# recorded path has neither property; it can only go away deliberately.
#
# Deliberately NOT derived from the tree, and that is not the WIRE-8 defect ("an
# assertion built from a copy of the thing under test"). The question this
# answers is "did something LEAVE", and no measurement of the current tree can
# answer it at any price — the tree only knows what is there now. That has to be
# written down to exist at all.
#
# Add a line whenever the step reports an executed file that is not recorded.
# Delete a line only in the same commit that removes the test, and name it and
# the reason in that commit message.
